# The `sdr` sidecar: tune a USB software-defined radio, return audio
# (docs/plans/SDR_RADIO_PLAN.md, S0b-ii).
#
# `debian:trixie-slim` rather than `python:3.12-slim`, and the difference is smaller
# than it sounds: the python image IS trixie — same rtl-sdr, same ffmpeg, same
# direwolf — so this rebase changes the INTERPRETER and nothing else, for +37 MB.
# It is forced by one fact: Debian's `python3-soapysdr` is a CPython 3.13 ABI
# extension, which a 3.12 image cannot load at any price (SDR_IQ_SPECTRUM_PLAN §3).
#
# THE DEPENDENCY RULE, WEAKENED ON PURPOSE. This image was stdlib-only; it is now
# APT ONLY, NO PIP. That is a real weakening rather than a restoration — the old rule
# refused "a Python SDR stack" by name and `python3-soapysdr` is one. What survives is
# the part that was doing the work: nothing arrives outside the distribution's ABI
# contract. Still refused — SoapySDR via pip (a second, differently-built binding
# beside the apt one), `pyrtlsdr` (it ships a forked librtlsdr, so two drivers would
# disagree about enumeration on a two-dongle box), csdr, GNU Radio (+759 MB, 242
# packages, and a terminal emulator on a headless machine), and a plotting stack for
# reduction the api's Pillow already does. Two exceptions, each earning it:
#   numpy     — the FFT librtlsdr deliberately does not provide. The only spectrum in
#               the rtl-sdr package is `rtl_power`, whose C clamps the interval to
#               `if (interval < 1) interval = 1` — one second is a floor, so ~10 fps
#               is not a flag away, it needs an FFT of our own.
#   SoapySDR  — the device abstraction that makes retune a register write on a LIVE
#               stream (no re-open, no blank canvas between bands) and an overrun a
#               return code. Under `rtl_sdr` an overrun is silent: libusb stops
#               resubmitting, the RTL2832U's FIFO drops, and no message is printed
#               for anyone to scrape.
#
# EGRESS-FREE by topology: compose puts this on a network declared `internal: true`,
# so the container has no route off the box. A receiver has no reason to reach the
# internet, and the network says so regardless of what runs in here.
#
# Runs as ROOT deliberately. The device nodes under /dev/bus/usb are root-owned, and
# the alternatives — a udev rule assigning a group, then joining that GID here —
# solve a problem this container does not have: it is egress-free, holds no owner
# data, and its whole job is to open one USB device. The GPU services join host GIDs
# because they must run as a non-root user for other reasons; this one need not.
FROM debian:trixie-slim

# rtl-sdr brings librtlsdr plus rtl_fm / rtl_sdr / rtl_power / rtl_test. usbutils is
# not needed — enumeration happens through sysfs in the supervisor, not here.
#
# python3 + python3-numpy come from apt for the ABI reason above: Debian builds its
# SoapySDR binding against the interpreter it ships, and a pip numpy beside a Debian
# one is two array implementations in one image. python3-soapysdr is the binding,
# soapysdr-module-rtlsdr the driver behind it (without the module the binding
# enumerates nothing), and soapysdr-tools is `SoapySDRUtil --probe` — the one-line
# answer to "does the container see the dongle" from the owner's debug console, on a
# box whose owner has no terminal (CLAUDE.md #10).
#
# ffmpeg is the encoder for the LIVE listening path: rtl_fm emits raw PCM, which no
# browser plays, and MP3 is what an ordinary <audio> element accepts from a chunked
# response it may join at ANY point — a listener attaches every time the tuner sheet
# opens, long after the session started (deploy/sdr/listen.py explains why that rules
# out a header-bearing container like WebM). It is a real ~150 MB dependency on an
# opt-in profile, taken rather than hand-rolling an MP3 muxer.
# direwolf is the reference soft-TNC: bit sync, NRZI, HDLC and the CRC for AX.25, which
# is the half of APRS worth nobody's reimplementation. It hands whole frames over a KISS
# socket and this sidecar does only the unwrapping (deploy/sdr/packets.py). Pulled in for
# the same reason ffmpeg is — a real dependency on an opt-in profile, taken rather than
# hand-rolling a demodulator.
RUN apt-get update \
    && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        python3 python3-numpy python3-soapysdr soapysdr-module-rtlsdr soapysdr-tools \
        rtl-sdr ffmpeg direwolf \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

WORKDIR /app
COPY deploy/sdr/server.py ./server.py
COPY deploy/sdr/listen.py ./listen.py
COPY deploy/sdr/packets.py ./packets.py
# The USB port reset — the one recovery for a dongle that has stopped answering, and
# the reason the owner never has to walk to the box for one (docs/runbooks/DEBUG_ACCESS.md).
COPY deploy/sdr/usbdev.py ./usbdev.py

# Fail the BUILD, not the first capture: this is the check that would have caught a
# sidecar shipping without its radio tools, whose only on-box symptom is a capture
# failing three layers away from the cause (the htmlrender image learned this the
# hard way — see its Dockerfile). SoapySDR and numpy are imported here for the same
# reason: an ABI mismatch between the binding and the interpreter is a build fact,
# and the alternative place to discover it is the owner's Ops -> Update.
RUN python3 -c "import server, SoapySDR, numpy" \
    && command -v rtl_fm >/dev/null \
    && command -v rtl_sdr >/dev/null \
    && command -v ffmpeg >/dev/null \
    && command -v direwolf >/dev/null \
    && ffmpeg -hide_banner -encoders 2>/dev/null | grep -q libmp3lame

EXPOSE 8000

# `python3`, not `python`: Debian ships no unversioned interpreter, so the name that
# worked on the python image is a container that exits immediately here.
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=5s --start-period=5s --retries=3 \
    CMD ["python3", "-c", "import sys, urllib.request; sys.exit(0 if urllib.request.urlopen('http://127.0.0.1:8000/healthz', timeout=3).status == 200 else 1)"]

CMD ["python3", "server.py"]
